# Generic .html -> extensionless fallback for every other page. Cloudflare
# Workers/Pages static-asset serving already does this automatically via the
# default html_handling="auto-trailing-slash" behavior (e.g. /foo.html -> 307
# to /foo) even with no _redirects rule at all -- these two explicit rules
# exist to upgrade that to a real 301 (permanent) redirect for correct SEO
# link-equity consolidation, and must stay LAST (top-to-bottom, first match
# wins; static/exact rules above must precede these dynamic/placeholder ones
# per Cloudflare's own redirect-ordering guidance).
#
# ":page" cannot contain "/" in Cloudflare's path-placeholder matching, so:
#   /:page.html          matches only single-segment root paths, e.g.
#                         /salinas.html, /about.html -- NOT /blog/foo.html
#                         (two segments) and NOT anything under /assets/...
#                         (assets never carry a bare ".html" single-segment
#                         name in this repo; all assets live under /assets/).
#   /blog/:page.html      matches only two-segment /blog/<name>.html paths --
#                         NOT /blog/sub/foo.html (three segments) and NOT
#                         /foo.html (wrong first segment).
/:page.html          /:page         301
/blog/:page.html      /blog/:page    301
